cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AtlasGB — every address in Pokémon Red and Blue, with the evidence for it"
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, a citation is appreciated but not required. What is
  most useful to the next person is a link, so they can check the evidence for
  themselves.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "The AtlasGB contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alchemy86/AtlasGB"
url: "https://github.com/Alchemy86/AtlasGB"
abstract: >-
  A machine-readable map of the whole address space of Pokémon Red and Blue
  (English, USA/Europe): 2,898 evidenced claims covering video RAM, cartridge
  RAM, work RAM, high RAM and the cartridge's own data tables. Unlike every
  other published Generation 1 memory map, every entry carries the evidence
  that supports it — named as an instruction operand in the cartridge image,
  observed to change on a running cartridge under a fixed script, or proved by
  a named invariant — and the entries with no evidence say so. Work RAM and
  high RAM are 100% accounted for, with no holes.
keywords:
  - "Game Boy"
  - "memory map"
  - "reverse engineering"
  - "emulation"
  - "Pokémon"
  - "dataset"
license: MIT
